cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived networks, please cite the paper below."
title: "Inequality and the Reliability of Science — simulation code and empirically grounded networks"
abstract: >-
  Agent-based network-epistemology simulations testing the equality effect:
  whether more equally connected scientific communities are more reliable.
  Includes the bibliometric network-construction pipeline (OpenAlex), the
  network variation method, the vectorized Bayesian bandit model, and the
  statistical analysis behind the paper's figures and tables.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/IgnacioOQ/e_network_inequality"
keywords:
  - network epistemology
  - agent-based modelling
  - philosophy of science
  - inequality
  - bibliometric networks
  - multi-armed bandits
authors:
